  "items": [
    {
      "name": "What's actually happening in your finger",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The tendon that bends",
        "your finger runs through",
        "a narrow tunnel",
        "",
        "When that tunnel gets",
        "irritated, a small nodule",
        "forms on the tendon",
        "and catches every time",
        "you bend or straighten"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Diabetes raises your risk a lot",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "People with diabetes are",
        "up to 4 times more likely",
        "to develop trigger finger",
        "than people without it",
        "",
        "It's also more common",
        "after age 45 and in people",
        "with rheumatoid arthritis"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Repetitive gripping is a trigger too",
      "char_file": "마우스_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Heavy manual work,",
        "tools that need a strong grip,",
        "even long hours on a",
        "keyboard and mouse",
        "",
        "can irritate that tendon",
        "sheath over time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "How to spot it",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The finger gets stuck bent",
        "and may snap straight",
        "with a pop",
        "",
        "Usually worse first thing",
        "in the morning, easing up",
        "as you move it",
        "",
        "The ring finger and thumb",
        "are hit the most"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Start simple: rest and OTC meds",
      "char_file": "온찜질_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "For mild cases, an OTC",
        "anti-inflammatory for",
        "about 2 weeks",
        "",
        "plus gentle finger stretches,",
        "is often enough"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Next step: a night splint",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "If the finger is actually",
        "locking, a splint that",
        "keeps it straight",
        "while you sleep",
        "",
        "is the next step —",
        "no needles, no surgery"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "A steroid shot works for most people",
      "char_file": "손가락_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "If it keeps catching,",
        "a steroid injection into",
        "the tendon sheath calms",
        "the swelling directly",
        "",
        "Surgery only comes in",
        "when that doesn't help —",
        "a quick outpatient procedure"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "closing": {
    "headline": [
      [
        "Treat it early —"
      ],
      [
        "trigger finger",
        "responds well to care"
      ]
    ],
    "tip": [
      "If your finger is locking in a bent position, get it checked within weeks, not months",
      "People with diabetes have a much higher risk — don't brush off a catching or popping finger"
    ],
